data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission report — \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (\\\"World\\\") and the empty string\\n   (`\\\"\\\"`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK).\\n\\n## How it was delivered\\n\\n- Single dispatch to `dev` (dev/d002) with the full mission spec.\\n- Dev implemented both files and committed `5ed6317` (\\\"Add greet function\\n  with unit tests\\\") on its own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`), based on `c2c400d`\\n  (matches the recorded repo base).\\n\\n## Independent verification (not just trusting dev's report)\\n\\n- Fetched dev's branch into the orchestrator clone; `git diff` against the\\n  base commit showed exactly the two new files, nothing else touched.\\n- Cloned a fresh copy of the repo, checked out dev's commit `5ed6317`, and\\n  ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself: 2 tests ran, OK,\\n  exit code 0 — matching dev's reported output exactly.\\n\\n## Judgment\\n\\nAccepted dev's reply (d002) on first attempt — verified evidence matched the\\nclaim with no discrepancies. No rework was needed.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

